      "content": "#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n#include <climits>\n\nstatic const int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\nstatic char buf[BUFSIZE];\nstatic int pos = 0, len = 0;\n\ninline char getChar() {\n    if (pos >= len) {\n        len = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n        pos = 0;\n    }\n    return buf[pos++];\n}\n\ninline int readInt() {\n    char c;\n    do { c = getChar(); } while (c <= ' ');\n    int sign = 1;\n    if (c == '-') { sign = -1; c = getChar(); }\n    int x = c - '0';\n    for (;;) {\n        c = getChar();\n        if (c < '0' || c > '9') break;\n        x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n    }\n    return sign * x;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n = readInt();\n    int s = readInt();\n\n    std::vector<long long> pref((size_t)(n + 1) * n, 0);\n    std::vector<int> row(n);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            row[j] = readInt();\n        }\n        const int curRow = (i + 1) * n;\n        const int prevRow = i * n;\n        #pragma omp simd\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            pref[curRow + j] = pref[prevRow + j] + row[j];\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i) {\n        const int rowStart = i * n;\n        const int rowEnd   = (i + s) * n;\n\n        long long window = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < s; ++j) {\n            window += pref[rowEnd + j] - pref[rowStart + j];\n        }\n        long long curMax = window;\n\n        for (int j = s; j < n; ++j) {\n            window += (pref[rowEnd + j] - pref[rowStart + j])\n                    - (pref[rowEnd + (j - s)] - pref[rowStart + (j - s)]);\n            if (window > curMax) curMax = window;\n        }\n\n        if (curMax > mxSum) mxSum = curMax;\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Integrating A's fast fread-based scanner, C's vectorizable vertical prefix-sum construction with SIMD pragma on the input loop, and B/C's OpenMP parallelization over starting rows yields a correct solution that minimizes I/O overhead while exploiting multi-core parallelism.",
  "notes": "Used long long for column prefix sums to avoid overflow on large intermediate values. The sliding-window horizontal scan per row is retained from C/A; OpenMP reduction(max) handles the global maximum across threads.",
